#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8ebce398-b228-51b0-8506-e0c6124478a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-6852" :question/problem "Find the differential for $f(x,y) = x^2 \\sin y.$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/id #uuid "bb3ab0dc-7e26-58f5-a0c2-564c01c77f2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6854" :question/problem "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the cone is $V = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3) & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi \\cdot 6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =12\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0c4816ed-fba0-5dc7-94ba-646b875d653d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6875" :question/problem "If $f (x, y) = xe^y ,$ use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(5,0) & ={e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x+5{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+5\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-5=-3, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+5\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "febc72d4-b1b8-52c9-a805-013b30695077" :question/math-academy-id "e-6876" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx  -1  \\,  \\Delta x + 0  \\,  \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3-\\pi ≈-0.141, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈-1(-0.141)+0(0.2) \\\\  & ≈0.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,0.2) & ≈f(\\pi ,0)+0.141 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0.141 \\\\  & ≈0+1+0.141 \\\\  & ≈1.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac0761e-892b-53e0-bd4a-bcb35229b775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xy-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446854} {:answer/id #uuid "592edaac-aa03-5270-a8be-982b5b3cf8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+({y}^{3}-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y+({y}^{3}-2xz)\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446858} {:answer/id #uuid "949f1307-08bf-5cc4-b984-37982aadf2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}y-2xz\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446862} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d94390-787f-5fc0-9917-5d0f985a5aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xy-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}y+({y}^{3}-2xz)\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446865} {:answer/id #uuid "f3201288-0ff0-5d05-8546-c32107c2bd04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xy+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+({y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}y+({z}^{2}-2xz)\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1d94390-787f-5fc0-9917-5d0f985a5aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xy-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}y+({y}^{3}-2xz)\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446865} :answer-field/id #uuid "6982bff1-d527-5b1b-a1cc-95bd4bd0cec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e237109-086a-53bd-a512-ebeaca53c3dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-167152" :question/problem "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{3}z-x{z}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =(2xy-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}z)\\,\\text{d}y+({y}^{3}-2xz)\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4828acff-c15d-5d8b-9aef-ef355a0e567c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282298} {:answer/id #uuid "488bc018-0350-58c4-baa3-b73fb7849aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282303} {:answer/id #uuid "5b56108c-83c5-51b0-97bc-ef1c90c49d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282464} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca7aaf3-036b-5d3c-81a2-2d24c2990bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282907} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1e2841-ac00-5d17-89b8-d50f0b0fa21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4828acff-c15d-5d8b-9aef-ef355a0e567c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282298} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc6259cc-71be-5ab6-b921-84982c5929c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d3c9249-0c86-56ad-b2f3-cb8e23eff378" :question/math-academy-id "q-167166" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{2y-z},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(-1,2,3)$ to $(1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={e}^{2y-z}\\,\\text{d}x+2x{e}^{2y-z}\\,\\text{d}y-x{e}^{2y-z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(-1,2,3),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(-1,2,3) & ={e}^{2(2)-3}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot {e}^{2(2)-3}\\,\\text{d}y-(-1)\\cdot {e}^{2(2)-3}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =e\\,\\text{d}x-2e\\,\\text{d}y+e\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(-1+Δx,2+Δy,3+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈e\\,Δx-2e\\,Δy+e\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(-1,2,3)$ to $(1,0,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-(-1)=2, \\\\ Δy & =0-2=-2 \\\\ Δz & =1-3=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈e\\,Δx-2e\\,Δy+e\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈e\\cdot (2)-2e\\cdot (-2)+e\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ≈4e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $4e.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5152f4ba-9807-5034-82d9-7afabc4856aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282388} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd83828-03a9-5df9-ad60-8d9dfa74963f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282755} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba6475b-7aa4-50c8-8d58-f5e9707f340f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283048} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccbfa59-804e-58a4-be45-da1121b77a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283056} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6928cb-ddf2-503d-a13e-222221fd3d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba6475b-7aa4-50c8-8d58-f5e9707f340f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283048} :answer-field/id #uuid "61486874-98c1-5a08-a0dd-be97962e4d20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "862d8f4a-ef1a-5220-a521-4d8cdae9c576" :question/math-academy-id "q-167170" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sqrt{{e}^{0.2}+0.1}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y}$ at the point $(0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{0}+0}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{0}+0}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{2}\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{2}\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{e}^{0.2}+0.1}=f(0.2,0.1),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(0.2,0.1).$\n\nMoving from $(0,0)$ to $(0.2,0.1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =0.2-0=0.2, \\\\ Δy & =0.1-0=0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)+\\frac{1}{2}(0.1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.05 \\\\  & =0.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.15.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.2,0.1) & ≈f(0,0)+0.15 \\\\ \\sqrt{{e}^{0.2}+0.1} & ≈\\sqrt{{e}^{0}+0}+0.15 \\\\  & =1+0.15 \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b0dfa1-a3bd-5d86-841e-767261c7fdb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Δf≈0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373014} {:answer/id #uuid "b518876a-d6a2-57b2-92cf-9d904e6dd10f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Δf≈-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373015} {:answer/id #uuid "6c65d1de-3197-52f8-9f96-cfeb62d0ce2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Δf≈0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373016} {:answer/id #uuid "6123d165-543d-5503-b3d6-b4c4dfd85d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Δf≈-0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373017} {:answer/id #uuid "98e43f2c-7032-55d3-ac19-6318a10d07a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Δf≈0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98e43f2c-7032-55d3-ac19-6318a10d07a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Δf≈0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373018} :answer-field/id #uuid "c754f0c6-e9f0-5f7b-a4f5-f0c361b3d140" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a5a0b5eb-1d35-5e16-8d84-c218ac09143a" :question/math-academy-id "q-37306" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+y,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(4\\pi ,8)$ to $(13,8.5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4\\pi ,8),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(4\\pi ,8) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi \\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4\\pi +Δx,8+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(4\\pi ,8)$ to $(13,8.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =13-4\\pi , \\\\ Δy & =8.5-8=0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (13-4\\pi )+1\\cdot (0.5) \\\\  & ≈0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $0.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e787ee42-8dd5-5f81-a556-22d32986eb68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392077} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8e18d9-4cc4-51f1-8ca5-ba40810743ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+2\\pi \\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392078} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b32074-be3f-570e-8a8c-a67860b18c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+\\pi \\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392079} {:answer/id #uuid "f31bbb1b-7a58-5dea-b3d1-6f97b42f5717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+16\\pi \\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392080} {:answer/id #uuid "2cec0944-acc6-5c0a-aa87-1d2bc54c98da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cec0944-acc6-5c0a-aa87-1d2bc54c98da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392081} :answer-field/id #uuid "6900708c-aacf-5586-b694-7d6a48ac06be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35be243b-50e1-5aab-aebe-0bcb17e84ebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-37308" :question/problem "Given a cylinder, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the cylinder if the radius is $r=2$ and the height is $h=4.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the cylinder is $V=\\pi {r}^{2}h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =2\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=2$ and $h=4,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(2,4) & =2\\pi \\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206720dc-5d29-5fe7-a935-d460c5f7fe4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}x}{2x}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{y}+\\frac{3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z}{3{z}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345638} {:answer/id #uuid "60e82843-b5bc-592b-8e8a-58c661752d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346192} {:answer/id #uuid "d57d43cb-3345-55f5-a646-6d8b9b7d7077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}x}{2x}+\\text{d}y+\\frac{3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z}{3{z}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347228} {:answer/id #uuid "e73bde83-05e5-5564-81d9-ce5141672b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\,\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{2y\\text{d}y}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{2z\\,\\text{d}z}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347388} {:answer/id #uuid "ee21595b-210e-5e7b-884a-9841287cbccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\,\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee21595b-210e-5e7b-884a-9841287cbccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\,\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347454} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd8b4074-6941-5cda-be03-7a1459620be4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a08547f7-2388-51c6-b26c-7a79df9eb29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-79742" :question/problem "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\,\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f3e588b-cf69-5990-aade-5d4d0d244a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393970} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1c30ac-f4e5-5cae-817e-6472dd651920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393971} {:answer/id #uuid "3d167f95-aa69-51e6-bc6b-a6d667c8c8f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{d}a+10\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393972} {:answer/id #uuid "c3493508-929d-51ff-8209-693da138770a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{d}a+15\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393973} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2f5502-e420-57be-b75d-d3ac6ab14ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{d}a+15\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d1c30ac-f4e5-5cae-817e-6472dd651920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393971} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a999ea8-f45c-57d2-a0a1-60c9a2283d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "385e16b4-f8da-593a-b039-318c70552c9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79745" :question/problem "Given a rectangular pyramid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular pyramid if the base is a square with the side of $a=6$ and the height is $h=5.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the rectangular pyramid is $V=\\frac{1}{3}{a}^{2}h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2ah}{3}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=6$ and $h=5,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,5) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6\\cdot 5}{3}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{{6}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =20\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "393a2da4-2037-5f88-af20-25566e93ee10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{d}a+10\\,\\text{d}b+2\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345839} {:answer/id #uuid "5f766058-5345-504f-969f-c6f41943d337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{d}a+5\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346176} {:answer/id #uuid "8c626268-e771-514e-9e16-2f37c28e6a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{d}a+5\\,\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346570} {:answer/id #uuid "bd042560-3b82-573a-bb03-933f8a2d73a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346994} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe3e38f-3a94-535d-a8d4-214ff917e54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{d}a+25\\,\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd042560-3b82-573a-bb03-933f8a2d73a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346994} :answer-field/id #uuid "001e58e4-393c-54c0-893b-8d317963f75b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb226681-0351-549f-b81b-c5875e8a6018" :question/math-academy-id "q-79746" :question/problem "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=2,$ $b=5,$ and $c=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the rectangular solid is $V=abc.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =bc\\,\\text{d}a+ac\\,\\text{d}b+ab\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=2,$ $b=5,$ and $c=1,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(2,5,1) & =5\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}a+2\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}b+5\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f3dee8-e6f4-5787-8395-50cb7a5ce3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{d}a+22\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446855} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbc47ca-c217-5961-8ebc-60818e4b7533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35\\,\\text{d}a+28\\,\\text{d}b+20\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446856} {:answer/id #uuid "418af1c1-d6d4-51bf-ada3-9317c8a8af10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{d}a+10\\,\\text{d}b+14\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446857} {:answer/id #uuid "8596556d-0399-5275-8336-5e8a62170257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{d}a+5\\,\\text{d}b+7\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446861} {:answer/id #uuid "a1659264-c9c8-589f-9fdb-0ef010eb62c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{d}a+11\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15f3dee8-e6f4-5787-8395-50cb7a5ce3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{d}a+22\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446855} :answer-field/id #uuid "91bbad55-b7c9-5018-bd2b-a6b22c055c21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e75bdad-f36e-527c-a1e9-527d230dfe09" :question/math-academy-id "q-79748" :question/problem "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=4,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7.$" :question/worked-solution "The  surface area of the rectangular solid is $S=2ab+2bc+2ac.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂S}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =2(b+c)\\,\\text{d}a+2(a+c)\\,\\text{d}b+2(a+b)\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=4,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,5,7) & =2(5+7)\\,\\text{d}a+2(4+7)\\,\\text{d}b+2(4+5)\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{d}a+22\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "617286e8-47ce-51b6-b506-3b48cff8cb06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498029} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd99149-aedb-5119-a535-5559ad7a90f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498093} {:answer/id #uuid "884b8e65-9503-5538-83b3-f52c4b72fe28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{d}a+\\text{d}b+2\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498114} {:answer/id #uuid "89575744-0951-5e71-9a75-60b9e81bb12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{d}a+4\\,\\text{d}b+\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498116} {:answer/id #uuid "cab3f89e-5562-5702-943e-6433f814978e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{d}a+\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab3f89e-5562-5702-943e-6433f814978e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{d}a+\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498250} :answer-field/id #uuid "361b4f31-81d9-5f43-b63b-1aa713ee6c5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1b5df81-7853-5e90-b2a0-96b74729c9c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-79749" :question/problem "Given a right triangular prism, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ if the height is $h=1$ and the base is a right triangle with legs $a=2$ and $b=4.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a given right triangular prism is $V=\\frac{abh}{2}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{bh}{2}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{ah}{2}\\,\\text{d}b+\\frac{ab}{2}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=2,$ $b=4,$ and $h=1,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(2,4,1) & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1}{2}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{2}\\,\\text{d}b+\\frac{2\\cdot 4}{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{d}a+\\text{d}b+4\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a096788c-853c-5498-9e98-f2c341faf5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123957} {:answer/id #uuid "f7033e0b-729b-5d85-9a5c-4f9b133f9ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123958} {:answer/id #uuid "1823c3eb-0c29-5698-8bd9-73b26d35b304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123959} {:answer/id #uuid "1b81ed15-8180-5476-bd0f-8480f3857e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123960} {:answer/id #uuid "4e2b4b0b-b7aa-5de6-8a35-a718cca8d034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1823c3eb-0c29-5698-8bd9-73b26d35b304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123959} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a51164-edc3-5bcd-b5d5-b6430f4e1533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3d2ae44-10d9-5db3-858c-8da3c9096267" :question/math-academy-id "q-79814" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{x}+xz,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(0,1,2)$ to $(-1,0,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =(y{e}^{x}+z)\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y+x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,1,2),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(0,1,2) & =(1\\cdot {e}^{0}+2)\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y+0\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y+0\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,1+Δy,2+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈3\\,Δx+1\\,Δy+0\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(0,1,2)$ to $(-1,0,3),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =-1-0=-1, \\\\ Δy & =0-1=-1 \\\\ Δz & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈3\\,Δx+1\\,Δy+0\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈3\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ decreases by approximately $-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18aa2d29-4200-55a9-9049-eec28d6ce46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345569} {:answer/id #uuid "28d8915f-3339-5227-a3ee-86c79928eb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345717} {:answer/id #uuid "39be8076-d1a4-53bc-beb7-69d5faf74820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345843} {:answer/id #uuid "e580e49f-e01d-5220-aa00-628de33ae96e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347372} {:answer/id #uuid "fb111822-7947-5e96-ad01-3bd29918f4a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18aa2d29-4200-55a9-9049-eec28d6ce46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345569} :answer-field/id #uuid "da7d86ef-4dea-5ade-8600-60a413066868" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a50b343-0303-5110-8cf9-6975a85c04cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-79815" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(0,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,\\text{d}y-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)\\,\\text{d}x+(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\,\\text{d}y-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y+0\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,0+Δy,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy+0\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(1,0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(0,1,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =0-1=-1, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1 \\\\ Δz & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+1\\,Δy+0\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (1)+0\\cdot (1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ≈1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032ef8bf-a149-5f5d-b9bc-54e6d8674bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.062" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345377} {:answer/id #uuid "3c56bb24-5e3e-5dba-9bd7-0f16e2f3edd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.066" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345861} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3bf950-dbc6-55c7-8257-4238683ae1b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.060" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346447} {:answer/id #uuid "85c38cb7-115d-538e-baa8-9d152e8db340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.058" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346514} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf00326-ca9e-5146-a772-c3778f9f8641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.064" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3bf950-dbc6-55c7-8257-4238683ae1b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.060" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346447} :answer-field/id #uuid "52c20e21-9157-5114-a78d-535633267fdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e921641-2f51-5af1-85b0-a27e011ac9c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-79836" :question/problem "Estimate $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.12)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{2}\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.12)=f(1,0.12),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1,0.12).$\n\nMoving from $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0)$ to $(1,0.12),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{3}, \\\\ Δy & =0.12-0=0.12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (1-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (0.12) \\\\  & ≈0+0.5\\cdot 0.12 \\\\  & ≈0.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.06.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0.12) & ≈f(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0)+0.06 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.12) & ≈\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0.06 \\\\  & ≈0+0.06 \\\\  & ≈0.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0516f7dd-9d93-57c6-ac01-af2cb388af77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345393} {:answer/id #uuid "2c46633a-f843-53a2-9bce-50673065b712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345747} {:answer/id #uuid "68f6bd37-5d74-5a8a-a983-e540fc0d5f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346261} {:answer/id #uuid "77700bc0-d51f-5b58-93c4-32ba10d18ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346400} {:answer/id #uuid "c5edcb38-7406-54f1-8a3a-1da16bc7f752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77700bc0-d51f-5b58-93c4-32ba10d18ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346400} :answer-field/id #uuid "e67277c2-ffd2-5937-8d1e-923e1b9e37f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d809b121-2117-5794-bb89-efcea5057754" :question/math-academy-id "q-79837" :question/problem "Estimate $(1.81)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.91)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{2}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n(1.81)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.91)=f(1.81,0.91),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1.81,0.91).$\n\nMoving from $(2,1)$ to $(1.81,0.91),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1.81-2=-0.19, \\\\ Δy & =0.91-1=-0.09.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (-0.19)+2\\cdot (-0.09) \\\\  & ≈0-0.18 \\\\  & ≈-0.18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.18.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.81,0.91) & ≈f(2,1)-0.18 \\\\ (1.81)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.91) & ≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-0.18 \\\\  & ≈0-0.18 \\\\  & ≈-0.18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03459f86-cd26-56df-bfd3-ae80dccdcdbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.967" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345380} {:answer/id #uuid "0e1e8fae-ee5c-5939-a4ae-b67a16f3db2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.965" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345464} {:answer/id #uuid "1134ab4d-4a2c-5eb6-80d3-c7193d047b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.961" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345498} {:answer/id #uuid "519e5c86-d04e-53b4-9169-038767ba67c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.970" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346054} {:answer/id #uuid "6af737dd-91d3-51d2-ab28-2ef9af78e57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.972" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03459f86-cd26-56df-bfd3-ae80dccdcdbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.967" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345380} :answer-field/id #uuid "f399272f-f649-5a0c-8d81-b24dff62d20e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c9a3a87-a14e-5269-82cd-f0a320dbf13f" :question/math-academy-id "q-79839" :question/problem "Estimate the value of ${e}^{\\sqrt{10}-3.2}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{x}-y}$ at the point $(9,3).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x}-y}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{\\sqrt{x}-y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(9,3),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{9}-3}}{2\\sqrt{9}}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{\\sqrt{9}-3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x-1\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(9+Δx,3+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{6}\\,Δx-1\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n{e}^{\\sqrt{10}-3.2}=f(10,3.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(10,3.2).$\n\nMoving from $(9,3)$ to $(10,3.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =10-9=1, \\\\ Δy & =3.2-3=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & ≈0.167-0.2 \\\\  & ≈-0.033.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.033.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(10,3.2) & ≈f(9,3)-0.033 \\\\ {e}^{\\sqrt{10}-3.2} & ≈{e}^{\\sqrt{9}-3}-0.033 \\\\  & ≈1-0.033 \\\\  & ≈0.967.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25aca136-de99-54dd-b945-23c1dcf34a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345693} {:answer/id #uuid "7beab84d-6621-58f0-affc-ca59f8977bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346434} {:answer/id #uuid "c41d60d5-79a0-517f-8981-2a0575f5c50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347046} {:answer/id #uuid "ecea43e1-5c71-5328-a98c-41f1756aade9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347441} {:answer/id #uuid "f7aa9fdb-97ad-5cc8-8020-7fcd4317caef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7beab84d-6621-58f0-affc-ca59f8977bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346434} :answer-field/id #uuid "725c2f1b-9770-5882-8e67-da604b7995d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6749d91f-49a8-5f4a-a9d1-89ed10459b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79876" :question/problem "Estimate $(1.06)^{4.1}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{y}$ at the point $(1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,4),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =4\\cdot {1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{1}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,4+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈4\\,Δx+0\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n(1.06)^{4.1}=f(1.06,4.1),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1.06,4.1).$\n\nMoving from $(1,4)$ to $(1.06,4.1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1.06-1=0.06, \\\\ Δy & =4.1-4=0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈4\\cdot (0.06)+0\\cdot (0.1) \\\\  & ≈0.24+0 \\\\  & ≈0.24\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.24.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.06,4.1) & ≈f(1,4)+0.24 \\\\ (1.06)^{4.1} & ≈{1}^{4}+0.24 \\\\  & ≈1+0.24 \\\\  & ≈1.24\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f28bab0-8456-5f5a-81a0-2d4c2c0ff063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,\\text{d}x+2y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393984} {:answer/id #uuid "0380e4d8-524c-5876-a2ba-f4f808b6ee38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393985} {:answer/id #uuid "ce023a6a-4ca2-5e23-87e9-456f69f65e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393986} {:answer/id #uuid "f094a75f-39e1-5051-97f6-2ffb4c8b2bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+2y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393987} {:answer/id #uuid "f56af906-7446-5099-8a95-5251df33c01b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f28bab0-8456-5f5a-81a0-2d4c2c0ff063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,\\text{d}x+2y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393984} :answer-field/id #uuid "76de9d7b-1d60-5af4-8f87-74b0c05b4000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4cf2d9e-3d03-57db-bef6-4b2ef0739dbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-79955" :question/problem "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\,\\text{d}x+2y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa4fcc7-abb5-598a-86aa-535a13940109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564012} {:answer/id #uuid "3235f6d8-fc17-53d1-96a2-97ded9b47bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy\\,\\text{d}x+2y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564053} {:answer/id #uuid "48108c9a-7393-5a6d-a4b9-1ee7f3a4618c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\,\\text{d}x+(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564088} {:answer/id #uuid "562d9cc7-78ed-57a2-b9df-268efd4fd357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564106} {:answer/id #uuid "d9dad321-6574-5221-b21b-bdaa701883b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\,\\text{d}x+2y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48108c9a-7393-5a6d-a4b9-1ee7f3a4618c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\,\\text{d}x+(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564088} :answer-field/id #uuid "55bae5ab-9b0c-588d-9a47-033bbbf8ef6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f3c5c64-c0f1-58d5-8582-f8f8e159dad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-79956" :question/problem "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y)=xy+{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y\\,\\text{d}x+(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72ff75da-b13e-5583-ae20-2ce0e2a55a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\,\\text{d}x}{xyz}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}y}{xyz}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}z}{xyz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446859} {:answer/id #uuid "81e483ab-3798-55cc-8300-27c841a9bb82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yz\\,\\text{d}x+xz\\,\\text{d}y+xy\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446860} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca16da6-7a8f-5ec5-ade1-d109e6b3501f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\,\\text{d}x}{yz}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}y}{xz}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}z}{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446863} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf3116a-63b5-5ad8-b1f5-843a36b5e2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y+z\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446866} {:answer/id #uuid "f807cb6c-01c1-5522-a5dd-56315c935102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\,\\text{d}x}{x}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}y}{y}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}z}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f807cb6c-01c1-5522-a5dd-56315c935102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\,\\text{d}x}{x}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}y}{y}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}z}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446868} :answer-field/id #uuid "102010b9-db98-5ea2-8e9e-7da7428fc2a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26a471f3-9b78-5070-a5db-c0478cd96f7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79957" :question/problem "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz).$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{yz\\,\\text{d}x}{xyz}+\\frac{xz\\,\\text{d}y}{xyz}+\\frac{xy\\,\\text{d}z}{xyz} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\,\\text{d}x}{x}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}y}{y}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}z}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e7b4730-07bc-55e3-a6a1-1f8f741572c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352147} {:answer/id #uuid "82af2898-1b6c-5362-bd25-0fa6ec45995a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352706} {:answer/id #uuid "a1fd631b-991b-54d5-9cc6-8f3cbf84de69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352953} {:answer/id #uuid "b1408a5a-b1a7-5eba-8e9e-add29f5b3b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353083} {:answer/id #uuid "bd42095a-e62b-516a-8666-20268ea4ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e7b4730-07bc-55e3-a6a1-1f8f741572c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352147} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb9582cd-856c-58b5-9f89-f922a1fb2623" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d42b8603-2969-573d-b945-d7e1061c7be0" :question/math-academy-id "q-86715" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({z}^{3}-y),$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(2,-3,1)$ to $(1,-2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2x\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{4}{{z}^{3}-y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{12{z}^{2}}{{z}^{3}-y})\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,-3,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,-3,1) & =(2\\cdot 2)\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{4}{{1}^{3}-(-3)})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{12\\cdot {1}^{2}}{{1}^{3}-(-3)})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{d}x-\\,\\text{d}y+3\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,-3+Δy,1+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈4\\,Δx-\\,Δy+3\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,-3,1)$ to $(1,-2,2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-2=-1, \\\\ Δy & =-2-(-3)=1 \\\\ Δz & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈4\\,Δx-1\\,Δy+3\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈4\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ≈-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ decreases by approximately $-2.$"}]}
